{"availability":"available","full":"BetaHuhn/MailPal","name":"MailPal","description":"Run your own email forwarding service on Cloudflare Workers to create unlimited email addresses on your own domains","category":"Other","language":"Svelte","stars":15,"forks":4,"created":"2026-03-20T21:55:23Z","updated":"2026-06-09T18:34:44Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mailpal.cc","topics":["cloudflare","cloudflare-email","cloudflare-workers","email-alias","email-forwarding","email-privacy","self-hosted"],"demo":"https://demo.mailpal.cc/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:32.273Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:32.273Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:32.273Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T14:47:32.273Z","stars":15,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A self-hosted email alias manager running entirely on your own Cloudflare account.","MailPal lets you create unique email aliases for every service you sign up to — so your real address is never exposed. When an alias gets spammy, disable it in one click. Every alias forwards to your real inbox, invisibly.","Unlike other alias services, MailPal runs entirely inside your own Cloudflare account. Your emails never touch a third-party server. Zero subscriptions, zero data sharing — just your Workers, your KV, and your rules."],"features":["Your real inbox, never exposed –","Give every service its own alias. When one goes spammy, kill it in one click, without changing your real address or losing your other accounts.","Total control, zero subscriptions –","MailPal runs entirely inside your own Cloudflare account on the free tier. No monthly fees, no vendor lock-in, no third-party servers ever seeing your mail.","Smart aliases that manage themselves –"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BetaHuhn/MailPal/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b0796c45ab9d24356077530250e0cfb61462c5281c3b3c7830b226ad3971c902","extractedAt":"2026-10-07